-- title:
--   Inertia naturality on the supersingular charts
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`. A finite set $W$ of places of the level-$M'$ function field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ is given, and `hW` states that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ` (the rational, affine geometric places whose value at the geometric $j$-generator lies in `ssJSet q κ`). The hypothesis `hle` provides the inclusion of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside Laurent series, into `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the unit reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` along $A$ with reduced field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (a valuation subring $R_0$`.integers`, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places, and the usual compatibilities), and `hR₀` states that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` belongs to $R_0$`.integers` and has residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Finally $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   Two families of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` are given: the Igusa family $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, and the supersingular family $O^{\mathrm{ss}}$ indexed by $W$. The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which characterises $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ at the point `lineInfty q` $= [1:0]$ as the set of $f$ admitting Laurent series $x,y$ with coefficients in $A$ such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ is nonzero and $f\cdot y = x$ as Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; `hIg`, which for each $\ell$ produces $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ` and $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty})$ along the level automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ produces a permutation $\sigma$ of the projective line with $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ pulled back along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equal to $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\sigma\ell)$ for all $\ell$.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that for each $s$ an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ if and only if it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, that for $s \in W$ and $f \in R_0$`.integers` which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ and, for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of the $R_0$-residue of $f$ at $s$, the difference of the image of $f$ and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, that each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every index $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   In addition, $\pi \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$ (`hπ`) and lies in $A$ (`hπP`); $\iota$ is a ring homomorphism from the field `GaloisField q 2` with $q^2$ elements to $\kappa$; and the coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21), the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables over $\kappa$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ` $-\,1$, is assumed to be a domain.
--
--   The geometric data consist of a semistable covering $\mathcal C$ of type `SemistableCovering q M' A W` — Igusa component charts $\mathcal C$`.CIg ℓ` with reduced fields $\mathcal C$`.FIg ℓ`, supersingular component charts $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` with reduced fields $\mathcal C$`.FSS s` over $\kappa$, annuli $\mathcal C$`.An ℓ s`, $\mathcal C$`.An' ℓ s` and attachment places $\mathcal C$`.xs ℓ s`, $\mathcal C$`.xt ℓ s`, subject to the structure's attachment, uniqueness and partition axioms — together with the identifications `hCIg`, that the integers of $\mathcal C$`.CIg ℓ` are $O^{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$; regular prolongations `RSS s` of $A$ with reduced field $\mathcal C$`.FSS s`, with `hRSS` identifying their integers with $O^{\mathrm{ss}}(s)$, `hCSSint` identifying the integers of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` with those of `RSS s`, and `hCSSres` asserting that the two residue maps agree.
--
--   The residue-disc data are maps `discS s` from places of $\mathcal C$`.FSS s` over $\kappa$ to sets of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and coordinates `coordS s` in `fieldBar q M'`, subject to: `hfamS`, that `discS s` and `coordS s` form a `DiscFamily` for `RSS s` with exceptional set the nodes of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` (each non-node $Q$ has `discS s Q` a residue disc with coordinate `coordS s Q`, and discs attached to distinct non-nodes are disjoint); `htransS`, the transport hypothesis, which for each $s$ states that whenever $g$ is a semilinear automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose base automorphism preserves $A$ and induces the identity on the residue field of $A$, and which fixes the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the $q$-expansion of $j$, then for every proof that $g$ preserves the integers of `RSS s` and every $\kappa$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $\mathcal C$`.FSS s` intertwining the residue map of `RSS s` with $g$, such that $\varphi$ maps the set of attachment places $\{\mathcal C$`.xt ℓ s`$\}_\ell$ to itself, one has, for every place $Q$ of $\mathcal C$`.FSS s` outside that set and every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the equivalence $P \in$ `discS s Q` $\iff g\cdot P \in$ `discS s (φ • Q)`; `hdomS`, that the domain of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` is the union of the discs `discS s Q` over non-nodes $Q$; `hpmS`, that the place map of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` sends every $P \in$ `discS s Q` with $Q$ a non-node to $Q$; and `hpmS_off`, that the place map of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` is constant outside its domain.
--
--   The hypothesis `hAn_tube` is the in-tube condition: for every $s \in W$, every $\ell$ and every place $P$ in the domain of the annulus $\mathcal C$`.An ℓ s`, and for every $f \in R_0$`.integers` which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the image of `jq` is regular and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the value of the image of $f$ at $P$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to any $a \in A$ whose residue equals the value of that $R_0$-residue at $s$.
--
--   The final hypothesis `hperm` is the node-permutation condition: for every $\tau$ in `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$), every $s \in W$ and every $\kappa$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $\mathcal C$`.FSS s` which, as a ring equivalence, is induced on the chart $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` by the arithmetic Galois semilinear automorphism `arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ`, there is a permutation $\varrho$ of the projective line with $\varphi \cdot \mathcal C$`.xt ℓ s` $= \mathcal C$`.xt (ϱ ℓ) s` for all $\ell$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions. First: for every $\tau \in$ `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ`, setting $g =$ `arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ`, the coefficientwise semilinear automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` attached to $\tau$, and for every $s \in W$: (i) for all $f$ in `fieldBar q M'`, $f$ lies in the integers of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` if and only if $g\cdot f$ does; (ii) for all places $P$, $P$ lies in the domain of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` if and only if $g \cdot P$ does; and (iii) there exists a $\kappa$-algebra automorphism $\varphi$ of $\mathcal C$`.FSS s` such that $g$ induces $\varphi$ on the chart $\mathcal C$`.CSS s`, that is, $g$ preserves the chart's integers and the chart residue of $g\cdot f$ equals $\varphi$ applied to the chart residue of $f$ for every integral $f$, and such that for every $P$ in the domain of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` the place map of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` satisfies `placeMap (g • P)` $=$ `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut φ` $\cdot$ `placeMap P`.
--
--   Second: for every $\tau \in$ `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with `A.tameCharacter π τ = 1`, i.e. whose tame character value at the chosen $\pi$ is trivial, and for every $s \in W$: the automorphism $g$ attached to $\tau$ induces the identity ring equivalence on the chart $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` (it preserves the chart's integers and fixes every chart residue), and for every place $Q$ of $\mathcal C$`.FSS s` which is not a node of $\mathcal C$`.CSS s` and every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'`, $P \in$ `discS s Q` if and only if $g\cdot P \in$ `discS s Q`; that is, each residue disc above a non-node is stable under $g$.
--
--   This is the inertia-equivariance step for the supersingular (Drinfeld) charts in the construction of the semistable covering of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ over a valuation ring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ above $q$: it shows that inertia at $A$ preserves each supersingular chart, acts on its reduction through a $\kappa$-algebra automorphism compatible with the place map, and acts trivially on the chart and on its residue discs once the tame character is trivial. It feeds the assembly theorem [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted), which collects the Igusa, supersingular and annulus clauses of the covering together with their Galois naturality.
